From d48dba919d3bb366ceadab3b4d8810237d7b36cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khaled <khaledchoucri@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:57:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 53/54] POC-16d: 19 rare BN6 programs, Omega Leader rematches,
 the Omega AI

- Programs (appended; names, texts, groups and shapes from BN6's StructArr_813944C and
  CompText873ECC8; effects ours, TUNE): Shield / Reflect / AntiDmg (B + back: a 30-frame
  shield, Reflect returns half, AntiDmg throws Swift), MegFldr1/2, GigFldr1, FldrPak1
  (lead Pokemon's raise the folder's Mega/Giga limits), AttckMAX / SpeedMAX / ChargMAX,
  HP+300/400/500, Battery / OilBody (Static-style type attraction in wild_encounter.c),
  SneakRun (a Repel that never runs out), Collect (+1 chip copy), AutoHeal (25% after a
  win), Tango (once a battle below 1/4 HP: +30%).
- Omega: a Leader rematch with the V3 Leader chip offers NORMAL / OMEGA before it starts.
  Omega: Leader's Pokemon +5 levels, tier-6 NaviCust and the Omega AI (aims ahead, counter-chips,
  punishes end lag, raises Protect/Detect against PAs and GigaChips, 15% faster, 20% more
  dodges, PAs at 2/3 and 1/3 HP). First Omega win pays a rare program; repeats a * chip and a
  record. pkbn.sav v6 keeps Omega wins and best times.
- Self-tests: PKBN_TEST_OMEGA=1, PKBN_TEST_LEFTB=frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FbWSqvcg6G5Gpw6ynvR5tJ
